{"name":"Chestnut Beach","hex":"#9a6844","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"chestnut","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An edible nut (technically a fruit) of the Spanish chestnut or sweet chestnut tree (Castanea sativa); also (chiefly preceded by a descriptive word), a nut from a related shrub or tree; or a similar nut from an unrelated plant.","In full chestnut tree: the shrub or tree that bears this nut, the Spanish chestnut or sweet chestnut (Castanea sativa); also (chiefly preceded by a descriptive word), a shrub or tree of the genus Castanea."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a deep reddish-brown colour, like that of a chestnut fruit (noun sense 1)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chestnut"},{"term":"beach","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The shore of a body of water, especially when sandy or pebbly.","A horizontal strip of land, usually sandy, adjoining water."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To run aground on a beach.","To run (something) aground on a beach."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beach"}],"entries":[{"title":"Chestnut","blocks":[{"text":"Chestnuts are the deciduous trees and shrubs in the genus Castanea, in the beech family Fagaceae. The name also refers to the edible nuts they produce. They are native to temperate regions of the Northern Hemisphere."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Ch%C3%A2taignier_120807_1.jpg/330px-Ch%C3%A2taignier_120807_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chestnut"},{"title":"Beach","blocks":[{"text":"A beach is a landform alongside a body of water which consists of loose particles. The particles composing a beach are typically made from rock, such as sand, gravel, shingle, pebbles, etc., or biological sources, such as mollusc shells or coralline algae. Sediments settle in different densities and structures, depending on the local wave action and weather, creating different textures, colors and gradients or layers of material."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Beach_at_Fort_Lauderdale.jpg/330px-Beach_at_Fort_Lauderdale.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beach"},{"title":"Chestnut (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Chestnut or castaneous is a colour, a medium reddish shade of brown, and is named after the nut of the chestnut tree. An alternate name for the colour is badious."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chestnut_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Chestnuts_at_Ljubljana_Central_Market.JPG/500px-Chestnuts_at_Ljubljana_Central_Market.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Chestnuts_at_Ljubljana_Central_Market.JPG/1280px-Chestnuts_at_Ljubljana_Central_Market.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Chestnuts_at_Ljubljana_Central_Market.JPG/500px-Chestnuts_at_Ljubljana_Central_Market.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChestnuts_at_Ljubljana_Central_Market.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Sweet_chestnut_DSCF0160.JPG/500px-Sweet_chestnut_DSCF0160.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Sweet_chestnut_DSCF0160.JPG/1280px-Sweet_chestnut_DSCF0160.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Sweet_chestnut_DSCF0160.JPG/500px-Sweet_chestnut_DSCF0160.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumb